<title>POLAND: OLAWA SIGNS $3.4 MLN EXPORT DEALS.</title>
<headline>OLAWA SIGNS $3.4 MLN EXPORT DEALS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish non-ferrous metals smelter Olawa SA has signed two export contracts worth $3.4 million, the company said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Olawa said that under the contract it would deliver zinc-based white paint products to Czech Bochemie Trading - Bohumin worth $2.2 million and red lead worth $1.2 million to German BBF Berlin.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
